      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit:  This is okay as-is, but consider returning the attestation_record by value in a std::pair or std::tuple.  C++ 17 structured bindings (https://github.com/AnthonyCalandra/modern-cpp-features#structured-bindings) make receiving such a pair/tuple and unpacking it on the caller side very clean, e.g. \n\nauto [err, parsed_record] \u003d parse_attestation_record(...)\n\nAnd, of course, move constructors and assignment operators (auto-generated in the case of attestation_record) make it efficient.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "1976a514272832f1876520dad38862dcadc73e5a",
